@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Output readability — sbx's principles in proveo's own idiom, across every command
' purpose: the delivery plan for making proveo's stream read like sbx's, without copying sbx's look
'   the vocabulary it amends ....... _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml
'   the design language ............ _spec/_conventions/tui-design-language.puml
'   the step lines ................. _spec/internal/ui/step-lines.puml
'   the design and its critique .... scratchpad of session e2da2921 (2026-11-11), summarised here
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS MEASURED (2026-11-11) ─────────────────────────────────────────
' One `proveo run claudecode` on a linked-worktree monorepo put 58 proveo rows
' on screen before the agent started; the longest was 235 columns. Workspace
' facts appeared in five places, and sbx's own create block then listed the
' mounts again. Sections were named by phase ("execution", "starting"), so
' "interface" printed between step 2/5 and step 4/5. Every fact carried a ●
' and most lines carried their own reason in parentheses.
' sbx's create block, in the same terminal, read better: sections named by
' subject, one item per line with a short result after " — ", aligned
' key/value blocks, detail dim on the next line, home-relative paths, and one
' closing outcome line.
'
' ── WHAT THE OPERATOR DECIDED (2026-11-11) ─────────────────────────────────
'   "adopt the principles, but don't copy the design verbatim"
'   scope ........ every command (run, init, adopt, attach/schedule, clean,
'                  ls/projects, rm, setup, uninstall, update)
'   sbx overlap .. proveo says only what sbx cannot: what sbx's create block
'                  prints (mounts, kit, image, CPU, memory, port publishing)
'                  leaves proveo's screen and stays in the run log; a
'                  re-attach, which has no sbx block, prints it. The image
'                  was a wrong premise; see decision D below
'   IDE attach ... one row on a live run; the JetBrains, Toolbox and VS Code
'                  text goes to the run log; a kept sandbox still prints all
'   fact rows .... keep the ● role dots and colours; align "key: value" in
'                  one column per block; detail dim under the value
' NOT CHOSEN: sbx's Title-case "Key:" column (the operator: not verbatim);
' capturing sbx's block (a hidden sbx prompt would hang); keeping both voices.
' The maintainer tooling behind mise tasks (since 2026-11-12 go test gates and
' two internal/ mains) is out of scope unless the operator asks.
'
' ── THE RULES (sbx's principle → proveo's rule) ────────────────────────────
'   P1 subject  A heading names the subject its lines describe, in one
'               lowercase word. sbx's own block runs under "sbx".
'   P2 item     A state is one line: mark, item, " — ", a short result.
'   P3 facts    Facts about one subject print as ONE ui.Facts block: role
'               dot, "key:", value; values start in one column per block;
'               a list value stacks under the value column.
'   P4 detail   Secondary detail goes on its own dim line, under the value
'               (a fact) or two columns past the text (an item). Never a
'               parenthetical sentence, never a second " — " clause.
'   P5 paths    Host paths on screen go through ui.Tilde. Guest paths,
'               every --print line and the log-only blocks stay absolute.
'               Mode flags trail in parentheses: (rw), (ro), (copy).
'   P6 what     A screen line says what a thing is or what happened. The
'               why goes to _spec, the how-to-change to the flag's help,
'               maintainer commands to the run log.
'   P7 outcome  A block ends on a ✓/⚠/× line only when it reaches a verdict
'               its facts do not already state: workspace ends on ✓ private
'               clone or ✓ mounted checkout; credentials ends on its ⚠/×
'               when one exists; run and egress stay facts only. Follow-ups
'               go dim under that line. (Amended 2026-11-11, decision A; it
'               read "a block ends on its outcome line".)
'   P8 marks    ✓ done · ⚠ attention · × failed · ● a role-coloured fact or a
'               running step (the operator kept the dots on facts).
'   P9 once     Each fact is said once per run, on screen or in sbx's block;
'               the run log keeps the full record. sbx's block names only
'               the kit-built image tag, so proveo's image is proveo's to
'               say (decision D).
'
' ── THE OPERATOR'S DECISIONS ON R1'S OPEN FORKS (2026-11-11) ──────────────
'   A result lines  A block ends on a ✓/⚠/× line only for a verdict its
'                   facts do not state (P7 above). NOT CHOSEN: an outcome
'                   line on every block; a credentials ✓ line in place of
'                   the login fact.
'   B host add-ons  Android emulator, host Chrome over CDP, Hermes Desktop:
'                   the "<add-on> — starting" live line leaves the screen
'                   once the add-on is up; each add-on is then ONE aligned
'                   fact in the interface block ("android: emulator-5554
'                   (AVD Pixel_9)", "chrome: …", "desktop: …"); progress
'                   lines and the Desktop install plan go to the run log;
'                   warnings stay ⚠ interface items. NOT CHOSEN: an egress
'                   fact; a new "host" heading.
'   C log paths     The run log's header records "home: <absolute $HOME>"
'                   once, so each teed "~/" resolves; rows stay as drawn.
'                   NOT CHOSEN: "~/" unexplained; a tee that writes
'                   absolute paths.
'   D image row     MEASURED (R1 round-2 review, sbx v0.50.0, a sandbox made
'                   for it): sbx's SANDBOX block reads "Image:
'                   sbx-kit-src:proveo-claudecode-0148841a44ae", the tag its
'                   kit build makes, and never names proveo's image. So a
'                   create run's sbx block prints ONE fact right before "●
'                   sbx create": "image: proveo/claudecode-browser:latest
'                   (published)" or "… (local build)" (posture.Image: the
'                   :local tag is the local build; since R2 carry-over d,
'                   sbx.ImageSource.Label: an image the host engine records
'                   building is a local build, and the run log's posture
'                   row reads the same label). A re-attach keeps its
'                   image fact from the receipt. NOT CHOSEN: the image only
'                   when non-default; the image in the run log only.
'
' ── THE OPERATOR'S DECISIONS ON R2 (2026-11-11) ───────────────────────────
' The design measured six real endings (clone, commits, push, crash, Ctrl+C,
' a failed removal); its critique found 15 faults. The operator chose:
'   F1 headings   "results" (how the agent ended, what came home, warnings,
'                 the closing line) on every run; "ide" ONLY when the
'                 sandbox stays, so a kept run ends on its IDE block.
'                 Nothing redraws "results" after "ide". NOT CHOSEN: the
'                 IDE facts as a second block under results (two subjects
'                 under one heading); "results" + "sandbox" on every run.
'   F2 home       what came home is ONE Facts block printed when the carry
'                 ends; ⚠ items follow it (settled by P3 and A). NOT
'                 CHOSEN: one ✓ per result; today's ● lines reworded.
'   F3 exit ×     proveo prints no × when sbx printed its own error line;
'                 × only when sbx said nothing, and it names `sbx run`,
'                 never the agent; an operator-chosen removal prints none
'                 (settled by P9 and the sbx overlap rule). NOT CHOSEN: ×
'                 as the last line (said 3 times); × first on every run.
'   F4 records    the egress-record and memory-log paths go to the run log;
'                 the OOM ⚠ keeps its path as a dim line. NOT CHOSEN: one
'                 "records" fact; today's two rows with ~ paths.
'   F5 log path   no log path at the end of a run (settled by P9: the run
'                 block names it). NOT CHOSEN: a dim log line under every
'                 kept ⚠; a "log:" fact closing every run.
'   F6 lift       a failed output lift KEEPS the sandbox ("kept: the output
'                 is only in it"); the launch receipt records OutputDir, so
'                 `proveo rm` lifts it. NOT CHOSEN: the tar recipe dim and
'                 the sandbox kept; removal as before, the output lost.
'   KEPT FIX      `proveo rm --stop` runs `sbx stop`, then carries and
'                 removes. The kept ⚠'s one dim fix names --stop while the
'                 sandbox runs, plain `proveo rm` once it is stopped;
'                 `proveo rm` without --stop refuses a running sandbox and
'                 names --stop. Nothing stops a sandbox implicitly. NOT
'                 CHOSEN: "`sbx stop`, then `proveo rm`" as two steps;
'                 teardown stopping every kept sandbox.
'   AGENT TAIL    the agent's last output goes to the run log on every
'                 run; its last 5 lines past sbx's own error line
'                 print dim under the kept ⚠ only when the agent drew on
'                 the alternate screen (?1049h). NOT CHOSEN: the log
'                 alone; today's 17-row block on every failed run.
'   KEPT IDE      "a kept sandbox still prints all": ONE Facts block under
'                 "ide" (ssh, jetbrains, toolbox, vs code, project), with
'                 DISPOSABLE CLONE, the carry-fetch recipe and the worktree
'                 note dim under project. NOT CHOSEN: the design's trim to
'                 the log; ssh and project only.
'   STOP MARK     how the agent stopped is a ● host fact, first under
'                 results ("● claudecode — stopped by SIGTERM"); "ending as
'                 on a normal exit" goes to the log; a clean or scheduled
'                 run stays grey. NOT CHOSEN: a ⚠ item; no screen line.
'   AGENTS.md     OUT OF SCOPE (critique item 15): the branches fact prints
'                 what the code measures, the seeded AGENTS.md snapshot
'                 included. NOT CHOSEN: an info/exclude fix in R2; a
'                 "only proveo's snapshot" row.
' Settled by the rules, recorded: the review and adopt commands go to the
' run log (E); "Ctrl+C again leaves now" stays on screen, an exception to E
' recorded here: it answers the keypress with what the next one does; the
' kept line of a failed run keeps the words "kept for diagnosis".
'
' ── THE OPERATOR'S DECISIONS ON R3 (2026-11-11) ───────────────────────────
' The design measured eleven init paths through the stubbed tmux harness
' (BEFORE: 26 rows and 8 headings on the main path, 2 drawn twice, 9 rows that
' said again what another row said, 1 false); its critique found 15 faults.
' The operator chose, or the rules settled:
'   F1 numbering  (rules) lines that stay drop "step n/N": a hand line reads
'                 "<program> — <what>" ("sbx login — signing in to Docker");
'                 live frames keep "step n/N · name · 3s"; git, GitHub and the
'                 prompt kit print no start line (Steps.Silent); verify leaves
'                 no plain line (Steps.Quiet). NOT CHOSEN: "step n/N" on
'                 every line that stays (2/4 and 3/4 with gaps); numbering only
'                 the lines that stay (the setup page's count would differ).
'   F2 how-tos    (operator) what leaves init's screen goes to `proveo init
'                 --help`, the flag help and _spec; init writes NO log file. A
'                 dynamic how-to (the prompt kit's rc, the sign-in command,
'                 "source <rc>") stays as the dim line under the ⚠ it fixes
'                 when the HOW-TO rule allows, or goes; never to a no-op Logf.
'                 NOT CHOSEN: an init log (a row per init, keep=20 shared);
'                 dim how-tos under every "later" row.
'   F3 verdict    (operator) the readiness verdict prints LAST, in results:
'                 "later", "not run", the ⚠/× check items with sbx's hint dim,
'                 then ONE closing line, "✓ host — ready to run" or "× host —
'                 not ready to run". Step order unchanged: a run blocker still
'                 stops the credentials and operator pages. NOT CHOSEN: the
'                 verdict under "sbx" with verify moved ahead of git (a blocker
'                 would no longer stop the later pages); a "host" heading with
'                 no closing verdict.
'   UNREACHED     (operator) a separate results fact "not run" stacks the
'                 chosen steps and pages a failure or a run blocker kept from
'                 running; "later" lists only what was answered later. NOT
'                 CHOSEN: joining them into "later"; no list on a failure.
'   HAND-OFF FAILURE (rules: P9 + R2's F3) a program init hands the terminal to
'                 that fails (sbx login, the release installer, the distro
'                 package, gh auth login) keeps its own error; init ends on "⚠
'                 init — stopped at <row>", exit 1, Reported. No "× <program> —
'                 <error>". NOT CHOSEN: tee its stderr (may change how sbx and
'                 gh see a terminal); always ×.
'   NO TTY        (rules) a question init could not ask (no terminal, not --yes)
'                 degrades without the operator acting: git identity,
'                 credentials, GitHub access and the operator name each keep
'                 ONE dim how-to. --yes is an operator act: its how-tos go to
'                 flag help. NOT CHOSEN: every how-to to flag help; only git's.
'   --yes GIT     (rules, a bug) --yes asks for nothing: hostGitStage reads the
'                 terminal through !d.NoPrompt. NOT CHOSEN: a separate commit;
'                 leaving it.
'   QUIT          one closing line: "⚠ init — quit at page n/N", with dim "host
'                 ready to run" when verify reached it (critique a8). NOT
'                 CHOSEN: two closing lines; dropping the verdict.
'   REVISIT       (rules: each subject once, critique 7; the R3 review) a
'                 revisit prints only what it changed: its hand lines, a fact
'                 or item no visit printed under that subject. "sbx", "git"
'                 or "prompt" redraws only above those lines, and a subject
'                 with nothing new withdraws its heading (ui.WithdrawSection).
'                 NOT CHOSEN: the whole block again (host twice, the shipped
'                 R3 draft); never redrawing (a hand line under git).
'   Ctrl+C        (the Executor's call, the task's "decide and pin") during a
'                 hand-off the program gets it; init stops after it like bash
'                 (wait-and-cooperative-exit), prints its blocks and "⚠ init —
'                 stopped at <row>", dim "Ctrl+C ended it", then re-raises
'                 SIGINT and dies of it (status 130), so a calling shell such
'                 as install.sh's stops too. NOT CHOSEN: a handler over the
'                 whole apply (a print from a signal goroutine races the step
'                 writing the same blocks); exit 130 alone (the second R3
'                 review: a caller reads it as handled and goes on).
'
' ── THE OPERATOR'S DECISIONS ON R4 (2026-11-11) ───────────────────────────
' Three designs measured the other commands (lists: ls, projects, version,
' schedule; kept: rm, adopt, clean, attach; upkeep: setup, update,
' uninstall); three critiques found their faults. The operator answered
' twelve forks through the interactive prompt; the rules settled one:
'   HEADINGS      (operator) no heading on any one-subject command: rm (list
'                 and <name>), adopt, attach, clean, ls, projects, the
'                 schedule listing, setup, update, uninstall. run, init and
'                 `proveo run` with no target keep theirs. A Section constant
'                 nothing names leaves ui.go. NOT CHOSEN: a heading only over
'                 a Facts block (upkeep F3 a); one heading per command named
'                 after it (F3 b).
'   FAILURE       (rules, R3's precedent) a command prints its own × item
'                 (sandbox.Item{Fail, Text, Detail}) through PrintBlock and
'                 returns backend.Reported: exit 1, main prints nothing. NOT
'                 CHOSEN: an itemErr type main prints.
'   LIST SHAPE    (operator, "match run's end") `proveo rm` lists each kept
'                 sandbox as a P2 item "<name> — <why>", its age dim; `proveo
'                 adopt` one stacked "to adopt:" fact, "(N new commit[s])" as
'                 R2's branches fact; `proveo attach` (no terminal) Facts rows
'                 keyed by task with the running value `proveo schedule`
'                 prints. Empty: "● no sandbox kept", "● to adopt: none", "●
'                 nothing running" (stderr). NOT CHOSEN: one stacked fact per
'                 list ("kept:", "tasks:"); today's rows trimmed.
'   RM STRANDED   (operator, "keep rm; retry line only") rm still refuses to
'                 remove while work is only in the sandbox; a failed rescue
'                 ends on "× <name> — not removed", dim "`proveo rm <name>`
'                 tries again", under the carried block's own ⚠ items. No
'                 sbx command, no bundle recipe on screen. NOT CHOSEN: `sbx
'                 rm --force` dim (it deletes the stranded work); the rescue
'                 recipe dim.
'   CLEAN HOMES   (operator, "output only; record it") no behaviour change;
'                 clean-lifecycle.puml records as KNOWN that --homes removes
'                 ~/.proveo while running sandboxes mount parts of it, with no
'                 liveness gate (--tools has one). NOT CHOSEN: a gate now.
'   ATTACH NESTED (operator, "item when nested") `attach -r` inside tmux
'                 prints one host item before tmux takes the terminal: "●
'                 tmux — nested read-only client", dim "the prefix twice, then
'                 d, detaches". An exception to the HOW-TO rule, beside R2's
'                 "Ctrl+C again leaves now": it names the keys that leave
'                 while help is out of reach. NOT CHOSEN: flag help only; a
'                 hand line on every attach.
'   LATER RUNS    (operator, "stack each run", P3 as written) the soonest run
'                 is the job's value; each later run stacks under it with its
'                 "in Nd Nh"; config and last sit two columns past the last
'                 stacked value. NOT CHOSEN: one dim "then …" line.
'   NO SCHEDULE   (operator, "both exit 0") the listing writes "no <~path>"
'                 to stderr and exits 0; the tick finds nothing due, logs
'                 nothing, exits 0, so a tick ⚠ always means a real failure.
'                 NOT CHOSEN: the listing 0 and the tick 1; both 1 (HEAD).
'   TICK HOME     (operator, "no false ✓; record fix") the listing compares
'                 PROVEO_HOME with the home the installed plist or unit
'                 implies ($HOME/.proveo: it sets none) and prints "⚠ tick —
'                 reads ~/.proveo/schedule.yml, not this home's", no how-to,
'                 in place of ✓; the install fix (carry PROVEO_HOME) is KNOWN
'                 in schedule.puml. NOT CHOSEN: the fix in R4; ✓ as at HEAD.
'   INSTALLER     (operator, "fix install.sh + setup") install.sh calls
'                 "$BIN_DIR/proveo" setup with no PATH prefix; setup's rc
'                 check matches this bin dir, not a marker alone (FOUND 9);
'                 R3's deferred installer lines ride along; installtest
'                 asserts the rc line once after two installs. NOT CHOSEN:
'                 change setup alone; leave it to the installer's owner.
'   UNINSTALL RECORD (operator, "by what left") one Facts block keyed root ·
'                 path · prompt · font, each valued with where it was; a fact
'                 only for a removal that succeeded; font as init prints it.
'                 NOT CHOSEN: by file; today's scope reshaped.
'   LEFTOVERS     (operator, "⚠ each, with its fix") from proveo's own records
'                 only: "⚠ schedule tick — still registered" with the dim
'                 command that removes it; "⚠ <name> — kept, its output only
'                 inside" with none; the closing "⚠ proveo — uninstalled; N
'                 left". NOT CHOSEN: saying nothing; asking sbx.
'   CONSENT       (operator, "every scope, one line") "› remove ~/.proveo, its
'                 PATH lines and the prompt kit? [y/N]", each scope only when
'                 present; the red Dangerf line goes (P9). NOT CHOSEN: the
'                 root alone.
' OUT OF SCOPE: Hermes Desktop's lines (they print inside `proveo run`), and
' every behaviour change but INSTALLER, NO SCHEDULE and RM STRANDED's text:
' every other exit status and argument rule stays HEAD's (the R4 review).
'
' ── TECHNICAL CALLS (the Executor's, from the design review) ──────────────
'   One shared helper, ui.Facts, aligns by display width, wraps a value at
'   its own column on the terminal only (the log copy stays unwrapped), and
'   prints aligned plain text in plain mode.
'   Lines that stay on screen drop "step n/N ·"; live frames and the run log
'   keep the numbers.
'   Each subject prints once, after the step that makes it true: the
'   workspace block after the mount plan, the interface block after sbx
'   create.
'
' ── WAVES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   R0  internal/ui: Fact, Facts, Detailf, Tilde, SectionSbx, the hanging
'       wrap; output-vocabulary.puml; unit tests. No caller changes.
'   R1  the start of `proveo run`, up to "● <agent> — starting"
'       (internal/run, internal/backend/sandbox): sections by subject, fact
'       blocks, the sbx overlap rule, the one-row IDE line, step lines.
'   R2  the end of a run: results, teardown, kept sandboxes, adopt/review
'       hints (teardown.go, results.go, pushed.go, sandbox.go's results),
'       the "ide" heading for a kept sandbox, and R1's carry-overs (a)-(g).
'   R3  `proveo init`: the apply stream, the result block, the verify step.
'   R4  the other commands: adopt, attach and schedule, clean, ls and
'       projects, rm, setup, uninstall, update, version.
'   R5  stray arguments: every no-argument command refuses one with one ×.
' Each wave: lint, both builds, the unit baseline, the named e2e tests whose
' anchors it moves (macOS; linux/arm64 where they run), the specs it touches,
' and this file's PROGRESS.
